#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:5
msgid "結晶の方向と格子面"
msgstr "Crystal Directions and Lattice Planes"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:7
msgid ""
"結晶の向きを指定するときは、格子ベクトルに沿った方向と、格子点を含む平行な面の組を使う。 前者は方向指数 "
":math:`[uvw]`、後者はMiller指数 :math:`(hkl)` で表す。ここでは両者を定義し、 "
"面の組の法線が逆格子ベクトルの向きで、隣り合う面の間隔が逆格子ベクトルの長さから決まることを示す。 "
"同じ指数を使っても、方向と面法線は一般には平行にならない。"
msgstr ""
"To specify orientations in a crystal, we use directions along lattice "
"vectors and sets of parallel planes containing lattice points. We "
"describe the former by direction indices :math:`[uvw]` and the latter by "
"Miller indices :math:`(hkl)`. We define both and show that the normal to "
"the set of planes points along a reciprocal lattice vector and that the "
"length of that vector determines the spacing between neighboring planes. "
"Even with identical indices, the direction and the plane normal are "
"generally not parallel."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:12
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`格子行列<lattice-translations>` "
":math:`A`、:ref:`分率座標<coordinates>`、 :ref:`計量行列<lattice-metric>` "
":math:`G`、:ref:`逆格子<reciprocal-lattice>` :math:`B`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: The :ref:`lattice matrix <lattice-translations>` "
":math:`A`, :ref:`fractional coordinates <coordinates>`, the :ref:`metric "
"tensor <lattice-metric>` :math:`G`, and the :ref:`reciprocal lattice "
"<reciprocal-lattice>` matrix :math:`B`."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:15
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:17
msgid "方向指数とMiller指数を定義し、格子面の組の法線が逆格子ベクトルの向きになることを示す。"
msgstr ""
"Define direction indices and Miller indices, and show that the normal to "
"a set of lattice planes points along a reciprocal lattice vector."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:18
msgid "面間隔を逆格子ベクトルの長さから求め、指数の共通因子が何を表すかを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Find the plane spacing from the length of the reciprocal lattice vector "
"and explain what a common factor in the indices represents."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:19
msgid "同じ指数の方向と面法線が平行になる条件を、計量行列で判定する。"
msgstr ""
"Use the metric tensor to decide when a direction and a plane normal with "
"the same indices are parallel."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:21
msgid "この記事では、断らない限り :math:`A` を基本並進ベクトルの組とする。"
msgstr ""
"Unless otherwise stated, the columns of :math:`A` in this article are "
"primitive translation vectors."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:26
msgid "結晶方向と方向指数"
msgstr "Crystal Directions and Direction Indices"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:28
msgid ""
"格子ベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol R=A\\boldsymbol u`\\ （:math:`\\boldsymbol "
"u=(u,v,w)^\\top\\in\\mathbb Z^3`）の向きを 結晶方向と呼び、:math:`[uvw]` "
"と書く。負の成分は数字の上に線を引き、:math:`[1\\bar10]` のように書く。 "
"向きだけを表すときは成分を共通因子で割り、互いに素な整数にそろえる。例えば :math:`[220]` と :math:`[110]` "
"は同じ向きを指す。互いに素な :math:`[uvw]` の :math:`A\\boldsymbol u` は、原点からその向きに "
"進んで最初に当たる格子点を指す。"
msgstr ""
"The orientation of the lattice vector :math:`\\boldsymbol R=A\\boldsymbol"
" u`\\  (with :math:`\\boldsymbol u=(u,v,w)^\\top\\in\\mathbb Z^3`) "
"defines the crystal direction :math:`[uvw]`. A bar over a digit denotes a"
" negative component, as in :math:`[1\\bar10]`. When specifying only the "
"direction, divide the components by their common factor to obtain "
"relatively prime integers. For example, :math:`[220]` and :math:`[110]` "
"point in the same direction. With relatively prime indices :math:`[uvw]`,"
" the vector :math:`A\\boldsymbol u` points to the first lattice point "
"encountered from the origin in that direction."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:34
msgid ""
"方向指数は格子基底の係数なので、同じ向きでも基底を取り替えれば指数が変わる。その変換則は :ref:`方向と面の指数の変換<lt-index-"
"transform>`\\ で扱う。"
msgstr ""
"Direction indices are coefficients in the lattice basis, so changing the "
"basis changes the indices even when the direction stays the same. See the"
" :ref:`transformation of direction and plane indices <lt-index-"
"transform>`\\  for the transformation rules."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:40
msgid "格子面とMiller指数"
msgstr "Lattice Planes and Miller Indices"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:42
msgid ""
"互いに素な整数の組 :math:`\\boldsymbol h=(h,k,l)^\\top` をとり、分率座標 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol s` が"
msgstr ""
"Choose a triple of relatively prime integers :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"h=(h,k,l)^\\top` and consider the points whose fractional coordinates "
":math:`\\boldsymbol s` satisfy"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:44
msgid ""
"\\boldsymbol h^\\top\\boldsymbol s=hs_1+ks_2+ls_3=m\\qquad(m\\in\\mathbb "
"Z)"
msgstr ""
"\\boldsymbol h^\\top\\boldsymbol s=hs_1+ks_2+ls_3=m\\qquad(m\\in\\mathbb "
"Z)"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:49
msgid ""
"を満たす点の集合を考える。:math:`m` を一つ決めると1枚の平面になり、:math:`m` を変えると互いに 平行な面の組になる。格子点 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol s=\\boldsymbol n\\in\\mathbb Z^3` では "
":math:`\\boldsymbol h^\\top\\boldsymbol n` "
"が整数なので、どの格子点もいずれかの面に乗る。:math:`h,k,l` が互いに素なら :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"h^\\top\\boldsymbol n=1` を満たす整数の組 :math:`\\boldsymbol n` があり、その :math:`m`"
" 倍を 考えれば、どの面にも格子点が乗る。このように格子点をすべて含み、各面に格子点が並ぶ平行な面の組を "
"格子面と呼び、:math:`\\boldsymbol h` をMiller指数として :math:`(hkl)` と書く。"
msgstr ""
"Fixing :math:`m` gives one plane, and varying :math:`m` gives a set of "
"parallel planes. At a lattice point :math:`\\boldsymbol s=\\boldsymbol "
"n\\in\\mathbb Z^3`, the value of :math:`\\boldsymbol h^\\top\\boldsymbol "
"n` is an integer, so every lattice point lies on one of the planes. If "
":math:`h,k,l` are relatively prime, there is an integer triple satisfying"
" :math:`\\boldsymbol h^\\top\\boldsymbol n=1`. Multiplying that triple "
":math:`\\boldsymbol n` by :math:`m` gives a lattice point on each plane. "
"Such a set of parallel planes is called a set of lattice planes. Together"
" the planes contain every lattice point, and each plane contains lattice "
"points. Using :math:`\\boldsymbol h` as the Miller indices, we denote the"
" set by :math:`(hkl)`."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:56
msgid ""
":math:`m=1` の面は、:math:`\\boldsymbol a_1` 軸と :math:`s_1=1/h`、すなわち "
":math:`\\boldsymbol a_1/h` で交わる。 同様に :math:`\\boldsymbol a_2` 軸とは "
":math:`\\boldsymbol a_2/k`、:math:`\\boldsymbol a_3` 軸とは "
":math:`\\boldsymbol a_3/l` で "
"交わる。成分が0なら、面はその軸に平行である。つまりMiller指数は、面が3本の軸を切る切片を "
"格子ベクトルの長さを単位に測り、その逆数を互いに素な整数にそろえたものである。例えば :math:`(110)` の :math:`m=1` "
"の面は :math:`\\boldsymbol a_1` と :math:`\\boldsymbol a_2` を切片1で切り、 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol a_3` に平行である。"
msgstr ""
"The plane for :math:`m=1` intersects the :math:`\\boldsymbol a_1` axis at"
" :math:`s_1=1/h`, that is, at :math:`\\boldsymbol a_1/h`. Similarly, it "
"intersects the :math:`\\boldsymbol a_2` axis at :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"a_2/k` and the :math:`\\boldsymbol a_3` axis at :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"a_3/l`. If an index is zero, the plane is parallel to the corresponding "
"axis. To obtain the Miller indices, measure the intercepts along the "
"three axes in units of the corresponding lattice-vector lengths, take "
"their reciprocals, and reduce them to relatively prime integers. For "
"example, for :math:`(110)` the plane with :math:`m=1` cuts the "
":math:`\\boldsymbol a_1` and :math:`\\boldsymbol a_2` axes at unit "
"intercepts and is parallel to :math:`\\boldsymbol a_3`."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:63
msgid ""
"分率座標は :math:`\\boldsymbol s=B^\\top\\boldsymbol r/2\\pi`\\ （式 "
":eq:`inverse`）なので、 :math:`\\boldsymbol g=B\\boldsymbol h` とおくと "
":math:`\\boldsymbol h^\\top\\boldsymbol s=\\boldsymbol "
"g\\cdot\\boldsymbol r/2\\pi` である。 したがって式 :eq:`lattice-plane-family` の面は "
":math:`\\boldsymbol g\\cdot\\boldsymbol r=2\\pi m` と書け、 逆格子ベクトル "
":math:`\\boldsymbol g` に垂直である。隣り合う面の間隔は"
msgstr ""
"The fractional coordinates are :math:`\\boldsymbol s=B^\\top\\boldsymbol "
"r/2\\pi`\\  (Equation :eq:`inverse`). Setting :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"g=B\\boldsymbol h` gives :math:`\\boldsymbol h^\\top\\boldsymbol "
"s=\\boldsymbol g\\cdot\\boldsymbol r/2\\pi`. The planes in Equation :eq"
":`lattice-plane-family` can therefore be written as :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"g\\cdot\\boldsymbol r=2\\pi m` and are perpendicular to the reciprocal "
"lattice vector :math:`\\boldsymbol g`. The spacing between neighboring "
"planes is given by"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:68
msgid ""
"d_{hkl}=\\frac{2\\pi}{|\\boldsymbol g|},\\qquad\n"
"\\frac1{d_{hkl}^2}=\\boldsymbol h^\\top G^{-1}\\boldsymbol h"
msgstr ""
"d_{hkl}=\\frac{2\\pi}{|\\boldsymbol g|},\\qquad\n"
"\\frac1{d_{hkl}^2}=\\boldsymbol h^\\top G^{-1}\\boldsymbol h"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:74
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"となる。2つ目の式は、式 :eq:`lattice-metric-volume` の :math:`G=A^\\top A` を使って "
":math:`B^\\top B=4\\pi^2A^{-1}A^{-\\top}=4\\pi^2G^{-1}` "
"と書けることから得られる。面間隔は格子定数だけで決まる。 例えば単純立方格子の立方基本胞では :math:`G=a^2I` なので "
":math:`d_{hkl}=a/\\sqrt{h^2+k^2+l^2}`、:math:`d_{111}=a/\\sqrt3` である。 "
":numref:`fig-lattice-reciprocal-vectors` の平行線は、二次元の :math:`(10)` "
"の格子面にあたる。"
msgstr ""
"The second expression follows from Equation :eq:`lattice-metric-volume`, "
"which gives :math:`G=A^\\top A`, so that :math:`B^\\top "
"B=4\\pi^2A^{-1}A^{-\\top}=4\\pi^2G^{-1}`. The plane spacing depends only "
"on the lattice constants. For example, for the cubic primitive cell of a "
"simple cubic lattice, :math:`G=a^2I`, so "
":math:`d_{hkl}=a/\\sqrt{h^2+k^2+l^2}` and :math:`d_{111}=a/\\sqrt3`. The "
"parallel lines in :numref:`fig-lattice-reciprocal-vectors` correspond to "
"the :math:`(10)` lattice planes in two dimensions."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:82
msgid "指数の共通因子"
msgstr "Common Factors in the Indices"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:84
msgid ""
":math:`\\boldsymbol h` の成分に共通因子があっても、式 :eq:`lattice-plane-family` "
"は平行な面の組を表す。 例えば :math:`(200)` の面 :math:`2s_1=m` は、:math:`(100)` の面の間に "
":math:`s_1=1/2` の面を挟み、 面間隔は半分になる。挟んだ面には格子点が乗らない。法線の向きだけを表すなら約分して "
":math:`(100)` と書けるが、:math:`\\boldsymbol g=B\\boldsymbol h` "
"の大きさと面間隔は変わる。回折では 反射ごとに逆格子ベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol g` "
"そのものを指定するので、:math:`(100)` と :math:`(200)` は 別の反射であり、指数を約分しない。"
msgstr ""
"Even if the components of :math:`\\boldsymbol h` have a common factor, "
"Equation :eq:`lattice-plane-family` still describes a set of parallel "
"planes. For example, the :math:`(200)` planes given by :math:`2s_1=m` "
"include an extra plane between two of the :math:`(100)` planes, namely "
"the plane at :math:`s_1=1/2`, so the spacing is halved. The inserted "
"plane contains no lattice points. If only the direction of the normal "
"matters, the indices can be reduced to :math:`(100)`, but that changes "
"both the magnitude of :math:`\\boldsymbol g=B\\boldsymbol h` and the "
"spacing. In diffraction, each reflection specifies the reciprocal lattice"
" vector :math:`\\boldsymbol g` itself, so :math:`(100)` and :math:`(200)`"
" are distinct reflections and the indices are not reduced."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:91
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"中心並進のある慣用単位胞の指数では、互いに素な指数でも式 :eq:`lattice-plane-family` の面が "
"格子面にならないことがある。FCCの慣用単位胞では、\\ :ref:`面心並進<centring-translation>`\\ のため "
"格子点の第1成分 :math:`s_1` は整数と半整数の両方をとる。:math:`(100)_{\\rm c}` の面 "
":math:`s_1=m` は :math:`s_1=1/2` にある面心の格子点を含まない。格子点をすべて含む面の組は、面間隔 "
":math:`a/2` の :math:`(200)_{\\rm c}` である。これは、\\ :ref:`中心並進のある胞の逆格子"
"<centred-reciprocal-lattice>`\\ で :math:`B_{\\rm c}(1,0,0)^\\top` "
"が逆格子ベクトルにならず、:math:`B_{\\rm c}(2,0,0)^\\top` がなることに対応する。"
msgstr ""
"For indices relative to a conventional cell with centering translations, "
"the planes in Equation :eq:`lattice-plane-family` may fail to be lattice "
"planes even when the indices are relatively prime. In the FCC "
"conventional cell, because of the \\ :ref:`face-centering translations "
"<centring-translation>`\\ , the first coordinate :math:`s_1` of the "
"lattice points takes both integer and half-integer values. The "
":math:`(100)_{\\rm c}` planes :math:`s_1=m` omit the face-centered "
"lattice points at :math:`s_1=1/2`. The set of planes that contains every "
"lattice point has spacing :math:`a/2` and indices :math:`(200)_{\\rm c}`."
" This matches the result for the \\ :ref:`reciprocal lattice of a cell "
"with centering translations <centred-reciprocal-lattice>`\\ : "
":math:`B_{\\rm c}(1,0,0)^\\top` is not a reciprocal lattice vector, "
"whereas :math:`B_{\\rm c}(2,0,0)^\\top` is."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:101
msgid "方向と面法線が平行になる条件"
msgstr "When a Direction and a Plane Normal Are Parallel"

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:103
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"同じ指数 :math:`\\boldsymbol u=(u,v,w)^\\top` を方向 :math:`[uvw]` と面 "
":math:`(uvw)` に用いたとき、 方向ベクトル :math:`A\\boldsymbol u` と面法線 "
":math:`B\\boldsymbol u=2\\pi AG^{-1}\\boldsymbol u` が平行になる条件は、 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol u` が計量行列 :math:`G` の固有ベクトルであること。:math:`G\\propto I` "
"なら任意の指数について 平行だが、:math:`G\\not\\propto I` "
"でも特定の指数では平行になりうる。したがって平行かどうかは晶系名だけでは "
"決まらず、基底と指数の組による。立方晶の直交慣用基底では、任意の同じ指数の方向と面法線が平行になる。"
msgstr ""
"When the same indices :math:`\\boldsymbol u=(u,v,w)^\\top` are used for a"
" direction :math:`[uvw]` and a plane :math:`(uvw)`, the direction vector "
":math:`A\\boldsymbol u` and the plane normal :math:`B\\boldsymbol u=2\\pi"
" AG^{-1}\\boldsymbol u` are parallel precisely when :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"u` is an eigenvector of the metric tensor :math:`G`. If :math:`G\\propto "
"I`, they are parallel for any indices, but even if :math:`G\\not\\propto "
"I`, they can still be parallel for particular indices. The crystal system"
" alone cannot determine whether they are parallel, because the result "
"depends on the basis and the indices together. In the orthogonal "
"conventional basis of a cubic crystal, the direction and plane normal are"
" parallel for any matching indices."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:109
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-crystal-direction-and-plane-normal`\\ の二次元の例では、横方向の "
":math:`[10]` を保ったまま基底のもう一方を傾けると、:math:`(10)` の向きとその法線が変わる。"
msgstr ""
"In the two-dimensional example in :numref:`fig-crystal-direction-and-"
"plane-normal`\\ , tilting the other basis vector while keeping the "
"horizontal direction :math:`[10]` fixed changes the orientation of the "
":math:`(10)` planes and of their normal."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:112
msgid "正方格子では方向[10]と(10)の法線が平行。斜めの基底では方向[10]は右を向き、法線は斜め下を向く。"
msgstr ""
"In the square lattice, the direction [10] and the normal to (10) are "
"parallel. In the oblique basis, the [10] direction points to the right "
"and the normal points diagonally downward."

#: ../../solid/crystal_directions_planes.rst:118
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"灰色の破線は :math:`(10)` にあたる線、:math:`\\boldsymbol g_{10}` はその法線を表す。 "
":math:`[10]` の矢印は格子ベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol a_1` の全長で描き、 法線の長さは模式的に示した。"
msgstr ""
"The dashed gray line represents a :math:`(10)` plane in two dimensions, "
"and :math:`\\boldsymbol g_{10}` is its normal. The arrow for :math:`[10]`"
" is drawn at the full length of the lattice vector :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"a_1`. The length of the normal is schematic."

